// THE POSITIVE CONTROL FOR `make asan-corpus`. This is issue #785's
// repro, kept here for one reason: it is a KNOWN, LIVE, UNFIXED
// stack-use-after-return, so a sanitizer sweep that cannot see this one
// cannot see any of them.
//
// WHY A GATE NEEDS ONE AT ALL. `-fsanitize=address` is not a property of
// the source, it is a property of how the source was BUILT, and the
// build can silently take the detector away. At `-O2` gcc inlines
// `pick` into `main`, the frame ASan would have poisoned never exists,
// and this exact program runs CLEAN and prints the RIGHT ANSWER -- so a
// 698-program sweep built at `-O2` reports a spotless tree with this bug
// sitting inside it. That is not a hypothetical: it is what the first
// sweep did, and injecting this program as a live control is the only
// reason anyone noticed.
//
// So scripts/asan_corpus.sh compiles THIS file with the SAME flag string
// it is about to compile the corpus with, and refuses to run the sweep
// at all unless the report in main.reports comes back. A quiet canary
// means a vacuous gate, and a vacuous gate must say so rather than pass.
//
// WHEN #785 IS FIXED, this file does not get deleted -- it stops being a
// canary and the gate goes red for the right reason. Replace it with
// another program that still reports, or take the whole positive control
// out deliberately and write down what replaced it.
//
// The bug: `pick`'s return type is its own trait bound, so the fat value
// is built over `t` -- the by-value parameter -- and returned. `t` dies
// with the frame; `self.base` then reads a returned stack slot. Dispatch
// is correct (the right `weigh` body runs); the receiver is dead. At
// -O0 it prints `1 0` where `11 40` is right.

Weighed = {
    weigh* = (self: @Self) i64,
}

Light = { base: i64 }
Heavy = { base: i64 }

Light.impl(Weighed, { weigh = (self: @Self) i64 { self.base + 1 } })
Heavy.impl(Weighed, { weigh = (self: @Self) i64 { self.base * 4 } })

pick ::= <T: Weighed>(t: T) Weighed { t }

main = (env: Env) Res<i32> {
    println(
        "{} {}",
        pick(Light(base: 10)).weigh(),
        pick(Heavy(base: 10)).weigh()
    );
    Ok(0);
}
